tier: mid-term
path: /artifact/colour-never-carries-state-alone-in-this
created_at: 2026-09-08T09:37:22.142396+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:68773fd1-2296-4527-b027-8d5d6c699ece] @ 2026-09-08T09:37:22.142396+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:e12ca220-5f82-4226-a2eb-9964701f03c4] @ 2026-09-08T09:37:22.142396+00:00

Colour never carries state alone in this UI: every state also carries a bracket glyph - [OK], [!], [X], [--]. A wall display is viewed at an angle, in sunlight, by people with colour-vision deficiency, through a greasy screen protector, so this is load-bearing rather than a nicety.
---
[node:cabf56d2-4b59-4f19-96f7-9388071c1086]
type: decision
tier: mid-term
path: /artifact/colours-are-derived-in-oklch-at-fixed-hu
created_at: 2026-09-08T09:37:22.262832+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> DEPENDS_ON [node:0bc7e618-9b95-4977-9fe1-f3a48759276f] @ 2026-09-08T09:37:22.262832+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:8a6a1300-bb21-4ae1-8d79-4957f245fc99] @ 2026-09-08T09:37:22.262832+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:e12ca220-5f82-4226-a2eb-9964701f03c4] @ 2026-09-08T09:37:22.262832+00:00

Colours are derived in OKLCH at fixed hue and chroma, walking lightness until the WCAG target is met, and then written out as hex. OKLCH is the design space and hex is the delivery format, because oklch() shipped in Safari 15.4 and color-mix() in 16.2 while the deployment baseline is 15.0 - so every hover and active value is precomputed rather than mixed at runtime.
---
[node:61c0030d-8bea-45cc-888b-113297483487]
type: constraint
tier: mid-term
path: /artifact/radius-is-0-everywhere-with-no-exception
created_at: 2026-09-08T09:37:22.386658+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> DEPENDS_ON [node:716987ce-f933-41b5-8c4e-590c09dc33bf] @ 2026-09-08T09:37:22.386658+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:e12ca220-5f82-4226-a2eb-9964701f03c4] @ 2026-09-08T09:37:22.386658+00:00

Radius is 0 everywhere with no exceptions, including inputs, chips and the scrim, and elevation is never a shadow: depth is a 1px hairline border plus one step on the surface ramp, with the card's 2px inset frame as the only ring in the system. Sharp corners are what make the HUD read as instrumentation rather than as an app, and a blurred drop shadow under a sharp-cornered amber panel looks like a mistake.
---
[node:6d6046fc-9f71-4b88-8cfa-381a0fe1bd32]
type: constraint
tier: mid-term
path: /artifact/contrast-floors-for-the-kiosk-4-5-1-for
created_at: 2026-09-08T09:37:22.506547+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:68773fd1-2296-4527-b027-8d5d6c699ece] @ 2026-09-08T09:37:22.506547+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:e12ca220-5f82-4226-a2eb-9964701f03c4] @ 2026-09-08T09:37:22.506547+00:00

Contrast floors for the kiosk: 4.5:1 for body text and every status colour on its surface, 3:1 for large text, icons and any border that carries meaning, and 3:1 for the focus ring against both the control and the surface behind it. Disabled text is the one role allowed below. The hairline border is deliberately below 3:1 because it is texture and never a carrier of meaning - anything that must be seen uses the strong border role.
---
