path: /artifact/the-monospace-face-is-source-code-pro-s
created_at: 2026-09-08T09:55:56.142557+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:e12ca220-5f82-4226-a2eb-9964701f03c4] @ 2026-09-08T09:55:56.142557+00:00
-> CONTRADICTS [node:ee768ade-394d-475c-92fb-e5c5b28e0efc] @ 2026-09-08T09:55:56.142557+00:00

The monospace face is Source Code Pro, self-hosted as woff2 from the LAN backend at weights 400/500/600, replacing both the Courier New placeholder in the accepted wireframes and the IBM Plex Mono the design system had proposed. It was drawn for code read on screen - dotted zero, a 1 with a full base serif against a tailed l and a serifed I, Latin Extended-A so Polish diacritics are real glyphs - and it is SIL OFL, so self-hosting is unencumbered. Its x-height is 0.486 em against Plex Mono's 0.516, so every arcminute figure in the viewing-distance table drops about 6 percent; the 20px body rule survives with margin and the 16px label size now clears the 5 arcmin comfort floor at 1 m only barely, which argues for the 20px rule rather than against the face.
---
[node:36e6377e-7d18-4de2-b827-8644f15bf56a]
type: constraint
tier: mid-term
path: /artifact/context-memory-graph-dump-is-marked-mer
created_at: 2026-09-08T09:55:56.268439+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> DEPENDS_ON [node:a17b142e-850e-4cdb-8d84-2689e75428a7] @ 2026-09-08T09:55:56.268439+00:00
-> HAS_FACET [node:c62c070b-e4a6-41b3-86f3-00ad5d96800f] @ 2026-09-08T09:55:56.268439+00:00

context/memory-graph.dump is marked -merge in .gitattributes so git never line-merges it. Git aligns similar blocks and shows only their differing lines, so a three-way merge of the dump can splice half of one node's entry onto half of another and produce a store that parses and is wrong. The documented recovery, agentic-memory sync resolve, does not exist in the installed CLI - sync accepts only status, dump and restore - so a conflict is resolved by keeping one side whole, running sync restore to rebuild the database from it, and re-capturing whatever the discarded side held.
